Top-level packages:
	jojo - The core functionality of the mod
		client - Client-side classes, that do not physically exist on a dedicated server. Meant to only be called on the logical client side. Classes like ClientProxy exist to call client-side functions in common code methods (on the logical client side only) without trying to load client-only classes (which would cause dedicated servers to crash).
		init - Registration of various objects for networking purposes: Minecraft objects (items, blocks, block entities, etc.), ROTP objects (in `init.power` - Stand and power types, ability types) and utility objects (entity data serializers, Neoforge data attachment types, etc.).
		mixin - All the mixin classes (they need to all be in the same top-level package). 
		network - Contains some of the network packets. Is being deprecated, in favor of moving each packet to the respective package.
		
		powersystem - Power, ability and action systems of the mod. Also contains the logic for Stand entities (in powersystem.standpower.entity).
		subsystems - Self-contained medium-sized systems, that usually exist for a couple specific JoJo abilities or features.
		customobjects - Helpers to create subclasses of some vanilla objects (damage types, status effects, projectile entities, explosions, etc.) with extra functionality.
		entityattachment - Helpers to add ticking and sync logic to Neo attachments that are attached to entities, as well as the "custom entity effects" system.
		util - Helper functions and classes to write less boilerplate.
		
		mechanics - Different somewhat self-contained gameplay mechanics and features (bleeding effect, Resolve mechanic, clothes feature, etc.).
		adventure - Encompasses the systems for the PvE content.
		
		command - Registration and implementation of console commands.
		config - Mod config system.
		event - Event hooks added to ROTP.
		modcompat - Utility functions to add interactions with other mods.
	
	jojoimpl - The implementation of each specific power/Stand, groups all that's relevant to each specific power type (abilities, projectile entities, Stand effects, etc.) together. 
	v1_21_4_stuff - The port started at 1.21.4 and was later backported to 1.21.1, in which some methods are missing. Replicating those should make potential porting to a newer version (for example 26.1) a little bit easier.

Terminology:
	Power - A collective of data that is attached to a Living entity and describes either its Stand power or "player power" (Hamon/vampirism/etc., previously called "non-Stand power").
	PowerClass (previously PowerClassification enum) - Use PowerClass#get to get a StandPower or a PlayerPower object of a LivingEntity.
	PowerType - An object that describes a specific type of power an entity can have (e.g. a single object for Star Platinum, an object for Hamon, etc.), has things like its default moveset, Stand stats, etc.
	
	Moveset - A map that contains all of the abilities the player currently has per each power class. Movesets are inherent to power types, but a moveset object is created for each power user entity individually.
	MovesetBuilder - Describes the moveset of a specific power type, and creates Moveset instances for each user individually.
	
	StandInstance - A data object describing the player's Stand (type, selected skin, parts taken away by Boy II Man, etc.)
	SummonedStand (previously IStandManifestation) - An interface for objects that represents the user's currently summoned Stand. Most commonly it is going to be a StandEntity, but StandType subclasses can override it to use their own class.
	
	PowerData - A data object corresponding to a power type (e.g. HamonData would contain stuff like player's Hamon stats). Is saved per each power type that the player has ever had, even if it's removed from the player.
		PlayerPowerData (previously TypeSpecificData)
		StandTypePersistentData (previously StandActionLearningProgress served this purpose) - Saves things like Stand exp and learned Stand skills.
	UnlockableSkill - An object that describes a specific thing the player can unlock (a Hamon/Stand/... ability or passive). Is contained in the MovesetBuilder - only one collection of these objects exists per each power type, so it's not meant to have a mutable state.
	
	Ability (previously Action) - a component part of a moveset. Each class extending Ability contains the logic of a specific ability. Because a Moveset object is created per user, unlike the 1.16.5 version, each Ability object is also separate for each player, so now you actually can store temporary variables inside Ability objects - still not recommended, but at least it shouldn't break multiplayer now.
	AbilityType - a type object that is registered in a NeoForge registry, allows to create multiple different objects of a specific Ability sub-class with different configs (kind of like a relation between EntityType and Entity - each EntityType corresponds to a subclass of Entity, and can create instances of their entity on demand).
	ConditionCheck (previously ActionConditionResult) - describes if an ability can be used currently - a boolean result of the check, and a message to send to the player if the check failed.
	
	EntityActionInstance (previously ContinuousActionInstance/StandEntityTask) - a data object describing the current "entity action" (most commonly an attack) that an entity is doing for multiple ticks. An entity may only have one action at a time.
	EntityActionType (previously IStandPhasedAbility) - an interface that can implemented by subclasses of Ability, to describe the logic of a multi-tick entity action (e.g. a Stand punch).
	EntityActionAbility is a convenience class that creates an action and sets it to the player, and also handles configs for the action phases length.
		StandEntityAbility subclasses it, reusing the phase length config fields, but overriding other methods to set the action to the Stand entity rather than the user.
	ActionAnimIdentifier (previously StandPose) - an animation id object, they link together each entity action and its model animation.
	
	EntityCustomEffect - Can be thought of as an amalgamation of a MobEffectInstance and an Entity. Attaches to an entity, can have ticking logic and contain custom data that uses SynchedEntityData system from Minecraft to sync.
	EntityCustomEffectType - A type object, once again, with the same relation to EntityCustomEffect as EntityType is to Entity.
		StandEffectInstance - Sublass of EntityCustomEffect that's attached to the Stand user; the primary goal is to implement persistent effects, which disappear when the Stand user dies, goes out of range or logs out, and which can also target another entity.

    OBB (Oriented Bounding Box) - new hitbox type that can be rotated in 3 axis.
    ExtendableOBB - OBB with extend/shrink logic (based on OwnerboundProjectile with ExtendableModel). Can be used to add hitboxes to animated parts (Star Finger for example).
